<title>UK: BNG says to launch 30 bln yen dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>BNG says to launch 30 bln yen dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>NV Bank Nederlandse Gemeenten (BNG) will launch a 30 billion yen three-year dual-currency Samurai bond next week, a BNG official told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>Bart van Dooren, head of international funding at BNG said the deal would be lead managed by Nomura and launch was expected in Tokyo on Monday.</p>
<p>The deal, aimed at Japanese retail investors, would be redeemed in dollars, he said. The pay date will be April 25.</p>
<p>-- Johanna Vellender, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5110</p>
